KITPro Server for Debian
========================

Docker Engine is an external prerequisite. The package does not install Docker
and never adds the API account to the docker group.

The alpha.11 to alpha.12 upgrade must be run with the package-bound
kitpro-debian-upgrade wrapper distributed beside the alpha.12 package. Raw
"apt install ./package.deb" and "dpkg -i package.deb" are unsupported for this
one transition because alpha.11's abort handler cannot recover cleanly from a
failed database preflight. Fresh alpha.12 installs use the normal package path.

For upgrades from alpha.12 or newer, the incoming package's preinst owns the
pre-unpack gate. It validates both databases with the installed release's
read-only verification interfaces and creates a root-only paired backup set
without depending on newly packaged payload files or policy. The incoming
postinst verifies that approval and pair before migration.

The dashboard listens on 127.0.0.1:8080 by default. For first setup, connect an
SSH tunnel to the server and open http://127.0.0.1:8080/setup locally.

Normal package removal preserves control state and all application data. Purge
removes the package configuration file but preserves control/helper state,
backups, logs, the service account that owns state, and /srv/kitpro. There is no
package action that implicitly deletes self-hosted application data or trusted
Docker ownership records.
